# Generated by `node tools/polestar.js profession gathering build` from tools/lib/professions/routes/cooking.json and data/forever. Do not edit: rebuild with that command.
guide forever/professions/cooking
title Cooking 1-300
category Professions
levels 5-60
zone Azeroth

# Cooking turns fish and meat into food that heals and buffs. It takes no profession slot. Most
# recipes here use fish, bought at the Auction House; to catch them yourself as well, the Fishing +
# Cooking guide levels both together.
#
# Cooking needs a fire: most towns have one beside the Cooking trainer, and in Forever every cook
# also knows Basic Campfire, a kit made from Simple Wood with Flint and Tinder that lights a fire
# anywhere.
#
# Ranks: Apprentice and Journeyman at any level from any Cooking trainer; Expert from the Expert
# Cookbook (Cooking 125), sold by Shandrina at Mystral Lake in Ashenvale and Wulan at Shadowprey
# Village in Desolace; Artisan from the Clamlette Surprise quest (Cooking 225, level 35) from Dirge
# Quikcleave in Gadgetzan.
#
# The route (crafts are about what it takes; yellow and green recipes can take a few more):
# Apprentice (1-50), from level 1:
#    1-50  55 Brilliant Smallfish: 55 Raw Brilliant Smallfish
# Journeyman (50-150), from level 1:
#   50-100 55 Longjaw Mud Snapper: 55 Raw Longjaw Mud Snapper
#  100-150 53 Bristle Whisker Catfish: 53 Raw Bristle Whisker Catfish
# Expert (150-225), from level 1:
#  150-175 28 Goblin Deviled Clams: 28 Hot Spices, 28 Tangy Clam Meat
#  175-225 55 Roast Raptor: 55 Hot Spices, 55 Raptor Flesh
# Artisan (225-300), from level 35:
#  225-285 72 Spotted Yellowtail: 72 Raw Spotted Yellowtail
#  285-300 18 Nightfin Soup: 18 Refreshing Spring Water, 18 Raw Nightfin Snapper

section Cooking 1-50

